  "notes": "The two square steel frames step inward at the star-shaped restaurant. Open X bracing surrounds the lift, and the upper deck carries the conch-stair pavilion and its thin mast. Reinforced-concrete footings and an open roadside dining terrace anchor the tower. The model follows the published 177 m height and the two public decks at 70 and 140 m above the original ground. The exact section sizes, paint color, glazing, furnishings and terrace detail are inferred from period photos. The full-sized tower is centered at the mapped memorial on Bolbro Bakke. Its signed facing follows the period view from the south and the nearby Middelfartvej alignment. Foundation corners and the dining terrace are approximate. The viewer shows the reconstruction for an explicit date during the tower’s lifetime. Native terrain, current streets and surrounding buildings provide the site context.",
